DEFINITIONS

Mods: The Minecraft mods or modifications to the game created and
maintained by XDPXI.

Fork: Any derivative or modified version of the Mods, including clones,
edits, or substantial reuse.

Significant Portion: An entire class, file, or code block large enough to
reproduce a meaningful part of the Mods' functionality.

You: Any person or entity using the Mods.

1. REVENUE SHARING

If you fork, modify, or reuse a Significant Portion of these Mods and
upload them to platforms that allow monetization, such as CurseForge or
Modrinth, the following conditions apply:

  - You must share 50% of all revenue generated by your fork with the
    original author (XDPXI).
  - You must contact the Author before monetizing your fork to arrange
    revenue sharing.
  - Upon request, you must provide verifiable records of revenue.
  - Failure to comply constitutes a breach of this license and may result
    in legal action.

2. DISTRIBUTION RESTRICTIONS

You may not reupload these Mods, or forks of these Mods, to hosting sites
that do not offer compensation to authors or maintain adequate control
over redistribution, such as PlanetMinecraft. Unauthorized uploads may be
treated as copyright infringement.

3. MODPACK INTEGRITY

Do not override the JAR files of these Mods directly in modpacks. The Mods
should always be downloaded from official sources, such as CurseForge or
Modrinth. This ensures users receive up-to-date and safe versions.

4. ATTRIBUTION AND LICENSE RETENTION

If you modify the Mods, you must keep the original copyright notice
intact. You may not change the license to something else; forks must
remain under "XD's MC License."

5. CODE REUSE GUIDELINES

Using small parts of the Mods' code (like individual functions or build
scripts) that fall short of a Significant Portion is allowed in other
projects with different purposes. You may not use this permission for
projects that directly compete with these Mods or copy their core
features.

6. LICENSE EXCEPTIONS

Exceptions may be granted on a case-by-case basis. Contact the author
directly if you need one.

7. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY

The Mods are provided "as-is." The author makes no guarantees or
warranties, and is not responsible for any issues, damages, or losses that
may arise from using them. Use at your own risk.

8. TERMINATION

If you break this license, your rights to use the Mods end immediately.
After termination, you must stop distributing, modifying, or monetizing
the Mods.

9. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION

This license is governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia. Any
disputes will be handled exclusively in the courts of New South Wales and
is intended to be enforceable worldwide. Disputes will first attempt
resolution under these laws, but the Author reserves the right to enforce
copyright and revenue-sharing rights internationally.

10. DMCA & GLOBAL ENFORCEMENT

The author can enforce this license worldwide by:
  - Sending DMCA or equivalent takedown notices on hosting platforms
  - Seeking recovery of unpaid revenue
  - Taking legal action under copyright law

FAQ

Q: Can I use this in my modpacks?
A: Yes, of course! You can use these mods in your modpack without asking,
   as long as it's downloaded from the official Curseforge or Modrinth
   link.

Q: Can I fork (clone the code) this mod?
A: Yes, you don't need permission, but if you monetize your fork you must
   split 50% of the revenue with the original author. You may not
   relicense the software, and you may not reupload it, or your fork, to
   sites that don't offer compensation to authors or maintain adequate
   control over redistribution, such as PlanetMinecraft.

Q: Can I use this as a separate dependency for my own mods?
A: You can compile against this mod and use it as a library, but you may
   not JAR it or bundle it with your mod. It should be marked as a
   dependency on Curseforge or Modrinth.

Q: Can I copy this bit of code I saw?
A: Yes! Just be respectful. You may copy small parts of this mod, such as
   individual functions or the build script, if used in another mod with
   different functionality. You may not copy a Significant Portion of the
   mod, or copy code from this mod to use in competing mods that serve a
   similar purpose.
